SUMMARY:ABCD Reads "Transcription" by Ben Lerner
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads "[Transcription](htt
 ps://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4726966)" by Ben Lerner.\n\n([RE
 SULTS](https://opavote.com/results/5098056250032128) of the poll for this 
 event.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**\n"From the “most talented writer of 
 his generation” (The New York Times)\, a lightning flash of a novel that
  is at once a gripping emotional drama and a brilliant examination of the 
 devices\, digital and literary\, we use to store―or to erase―our memor
 ies.\nThe narrator of Ben Lerner’s new novel has traveled to Providence\
 , Rhode Island\, where he is to conduct what will be the final published i
 nterview with Thomas\, his ninety-year-old mentor and the father of his co
 llege friend\, Max. Thomas is a giant in the arts who seems to hail “fro
 m the future and the past simultaneously” and who “reenchants the air
 ” when he speaks. But the narrator drops his smartphone in the hotel sin
 k. He arrives at Thomas’s house with no recording device\, a fact he is 
 mysteriously unable to confess." (from [Goodreads](https://www.goodreads.c
 om/en/book/show/231387262-transcription))\n\n"An emotional drama and an ex
 amination of the devices\, digital and literary\, we use to store—or to 
 erase—our memories." (from [BookMarks](https://bookmarks.reviews/reviews
 /transcription-2/))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to arriv
 e 30 minutes before the event and stay 30 minutes or longer afterward to c
 onnect with other attendees outside the book talk.\n\nPlease ensure you ha
 ve read the book before attending (though finishing any book is not a barr
 ier to participating\, as long as you don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst-time 
 attendees can join for free. If the event is full\, we maintain an unoffic
 ial waitlist. Please send [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/members/5529519
 2/) a direct message for more information\, in either case.\n\nWe request 
 a $3 contribution from regular attendees to help cover our monthly meetup 
 costs.\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each event\, we wil
 l ask for nominees for our next book. If you have a good one in mind\, ple
 ase ensure it is between 200-400 pages long\, available from the Toronto P
 ublic Library\, and counts as contemporary literary fiction (though these 
 are not hard and fast rules). When enough nominees are collected\, Michael
  will send the members a direct message with a link where you can vote.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/a-book-club-downtown-abcd/events/3155
 20207/
