SUMMARY:ABCD Reads Body Language by Meg Howrey
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads ***[Body Language](h
 ttps://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4801989)*** by Meg Howrey.\n([
 RESULTS](https://opavote.com/results/6325601387675648) of the poll for thi
 s event.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**\n"Sloane\, a former actress now work
 ing as a therapist\, is determined to find a meaningful way through menopa
 use\, away from marketing schemes\, possibly with the aid of psychedelics.
  Her sister Laurel is managing her own growing rage and restlessness while
  engaging in work at an environmental non-profit and raising teenagers. Na
 nette\, the youngest\, has answered a long-delayed religious calling and i
 s living as a Novice in a convent. All three lives will be further disrupt
 ed when Sloane receives a call summoning her to their mother’s house\, L
 aurel discovers possible evidence of her husband’s infidelity\, and Nane
 tte finds herself in the middle of a media frenzy after a spontaneous act 
 of public prayer.\nSoon\, all three are reunited under their mother’s ro
 of\, and no one can seem to agree about anything beyond the Barbara has de
 mentia\, as did her mother and sister before her. Will it be an opportunit
 y for the closed door of their very private mother’s inner life to crack
  open? A lesson in care\; a shared responsibility that will be the making 
 of this family\, divided by large age gaps\, parental divorce\, and temper
 ament? Or will a stunning revelation upend not only their mother’s remai
 ning time\, but divide the sisters permanently?\nWith razor-sharp prose an
 d undeniable humor\, acclaimed author Meg Howrey brings an American family
  in the midst of a painful crisis to unforgettable life\, interrogating me
 mory and emotional inheritance\, the right of a woman’s autonomy\, and t
 he indelible bonds even the most disparate of sisters can share." (from [G
 oodreads](https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/244709885-body-language))
 \n\n"Howrey is a reliably beautiful stylist\, and her slyly funny prose an
 d blade-sharp insights into human behavior really should put her in the sa
 me conversation as writers like Ann Patchett and Barbara Kingsolver. Thoug
 h this novel hits some familiar beats\, Howrey manages to haul in plenty o
 f shimmering pearls on the perils and joys of womanhood—whatever that me
 ans.\nA comfort meal of a novel: poignant and prismatic." (from [Kirkus](h
 ttps://www.kirkusreviews.com/book-reviews/meg-howrey/body-language-4/))\n\
 n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to arrive 30 minutes before th
 e event and stay 30 minutes or longer afterward to connect with other atte
 ndees outside the book talk.\n\nPlease ensure you have read the book befor
 e attending (though finishing any book is not a barrier to participating\,
  as long as you don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst-time attendees can join for
  free. If the event is full\, we maintain an unofficial waitlist. Please s
 end [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/members/55295192/) a direct message f
 or more information\, in either case.\n\nWe request a $3 contribution from
  regular attendees to help cover our monthly meetup costs.\n\n**:: ABOUT O
 UR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each event\, we will ask for nominees for
  our next book. If you have a good one in mind\, please ensure it is betwe
 en 200-400 pages long\, available from the Toronto Public Library\, and co
 unts as contemporary literary fiction (though these are not hard and fast 
 rules). When enough nominees are collected\, Michael will send the members
  a direct message with a link where you can vote.
